and the\nper-athlete context (facts, date) is a second, uncached block after it, so a\n`save_fact` does not evict the instructions from cache."}}}
{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01RSDXBfDn8DjiRtScdxSgTi","type":"tool_result","content":"The file /private/tmp/h-T7vHgu/README.md has been updated successfully."}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"a1723dc6-ae13-40ff-bd3e-920f18199787","uuid":"06a471e6-7fe5-43ac-841d-0abca7dd369c","timestamp":"2026-10-27T05:30:18.381Z","tool_use_result":{"filePath":"/private/tmp/h-T7vHgu/README.md","oldString":"Requires Python 3.11+ and `pip install anthropic`. Prompt caching is on: the system\nprompt carries a `cache_control` marker so the tool-loop rounds and follow-up\nmessages inside the 5-minute window read it from cache.","newString":"Requires Python 3.11+ and `pip install anthropic`. Prompt caching is on: the static\ncoaching instructions are the cached system block (`cache_control` marker), and the\nper-athlete context (facts, date) is a second, uncached block after it, so a\n`save_fact` does not evict the instructions from cache.","originalFile":"# pace-bot\n\nA coaching chat bot on Claude for a small running/cycling club. It is stateless\nby design: each message rebuilds the system prompt (coaching rules + the athlete's\nprofile, zones, goal and long-term facts from `data/athletes.json`), picks the tools\nthe message might need (`save_fact` and `log_session` always, planning or race tools\nwhen keywords match) and runs a short tool-use loop. `save_fact` is how the bot\nremembers durable things an athlete tells it; the next message sees the fact in\nits system prompt. Every API call appends its `usage` object to `logs/usage.jsonl`.\n\nRun it locally with `COACH_ANTHROPIC_KEY=sk-ant-... python3 bot.py 42` and type\nmessages on stdin (the Telegram long-polling transport, which needs\n`COACH_TELEGRAM_TOKEN`, lives in a separate deploy repo and just calls `reply()`).\nRequires Python 3.11+ and `pip install anthropic`. Prompt caching is on: the system\nprompt carries a `cache_control` marker so the tool-loop rounds and follow-up\nmessages inside the 5-minute window read it from cache.\n","structuredPatch":[{"oldStart":11,"oldLines":6,"newStart":11,"newLines":7,"lines":[" Run it locally with `COACH_ANTHROPIC_KEY=sk-ant-... python3 bot.py 42` and type"," messages on stdin (the Telegram long-polling transport, which needs"," `COACH_TELEGRAM_TOKEN`, lives in a separate deploy repo and just calls `reply()`).","-Requires Python 3.11+ and `pip install anthropic`. Prompt caching is on: the system","-prompt carries a `cache_control` marker so the tool-loop rounds and follow-up","-messages inside the 5-minute window read it from cache.","+Requires Python 3.11+ and `pip install anthropic`. Prompt caching is on: the static","+coaching instructions are the cached system block (`cache_control` marker), and the","+per-athlete context (facts, date) is a second, uncached block after it, so a","+`save_fact` does not evict the instructions from cache."]}],"userModified":false,"replaceAll":false,"contentNotInModelContext":true},"tool_result_meta":[{"id":"toolu_01RSDXBfDn8DjiRtScdxSgTi","permission_decision":{"decision":"accept","source":"config","reason_type":"mode"}}]}
{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-haiku-5-5","id":"msg_011CgSC6rd77pytrXJtghrM2","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_01GyTtRNkjatE1eHFtpo8LW8","name":"Write","input":{"file_path":"/private/tmp/h-T7vHgu/ANSWER.md","content":"# Answer: save_fact was evicting the static prompt from cache\n\n## Cause\n\n`build_system()` in `bot.py` put the coaching instructions and the per-athlete\ncontext (including `facts`) into one text block and marked the whole block with\n`cache_control`. Every `save_fact` changes `facts`, which changes the cached prefix,\nso the next call wrote the whole block again (`cache_creation_input_tokens` ~1100,\n`cache_read_input_tokens: 0`). That is the pattern in `logs/usage.jsonl`.\n\n## What changed\n\n- `bot.py`, `build_system()`: the system prompt is now two blocks.\n  1. `INSTRUCTIONS`, static, with `cache_control: ephemeral`. This is the cached prefix.\n  2. `athlete_context(a, today)`, without a marker. Facts and today's date live here,\n     after the breakpoint, so a new fact or a new day only changes this tail.\n- `README.md`: the caching paragraph now describes the two-block layout.\n\nNo other behaviour changed: tool selection, the tool loop, storage and logging are as before.\n\n## Checks\n\nRun locally without the API (no requests sent, `data/athletes.json` not written):\n\n- The static block is byte-identical before and after appending a fact to the athlete in memory.\n- The context block does contain the new fact.\n- The static block is still identical on the next day with the same facts.\n- Only the static block carries `cache_control`.\n\n## Not verified / to check in the next logs\n\n- **Minimum cacheable length.** Sonnet caches only prefixes of about 1024 tokens or more.\n  The static instructions plus the core tools are roughly 1000 tokens by my estimate\n  (the old full block read ~1090 tokens). If the first real calls after this change show\n  `cache_creation_input_tokens: 0` and `input_tokens` ~1000 on every call, the static\n  part is under the minimum. In that case it needs to be padded with real content or\n  the cache dropped; I did not pad it.\n- **Tool set in the prefix.** Tools come before system in the cache prefix, and\n  `select_tools()` changes the tool list by keyword (e.g. adding `plan_week` or\n  `predict_race`). A message that adds a tool group still misses the cache. That is\n  separate from `save_fact`, and NOTES.md says the keyword filter is worth keeping, so I\n  left it. Moving the marker to the last tool would not fix it: the group change still\n  alters the prefix.\n\nI did not call the API, deploy, or send anything anywhere.\n"},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":421,"cache_read_input_tokens":32052,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":421},"output_tokens":16,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"global","speed":"standard"},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"a1723dc6-ae13-40ff-bd3e-920f18199787","uuid":"815d4264-0cd5-4749-9ba7-9a0087199850","timestamp":"2026-10-27T05:30:23.242Z","request_id":"req_011CgSC6rNj6is21G8d6EaVd","wire_tool_inputs":{"toolu_01GyTtRNkjatE1eHFtpo8LW8":{"file_path":"/private/tmp/h-T7vHgu/ANSWER.md","content":"# Answer: save_fact was evicting the static prompt from cache\n\n## Cause\n\n`build_system()` in `bot.py` put the coaching instructions and the per-athlete\ncontext (including `facts`) into one text block and marked the whole block with\n`cache_control`. Every `save_fact` changes `facts`, which changes the cached prefix,\nso the next call wrote the whole block again (`cache_creation_input_tokens` ~1100,\n`cache_read_input_tokens: 0`). That is the pattern in `logs/usage.jsonl`.\n\n## What changed\n\n- `bot.py`, `build_system()`: the system prompt is now two blocks.\n  1. `INSTRUCTIONS`, static, with `cache_control: ephemeral`. This is the cached prefix.\n  2. `athlete_context(a, today)`, without a marker. Facts and today's date live here,\n     after the breakpoint, so a new fact or a new day only changes this tail.\n- `README.md`: the caching paragraph now describes the two-block layout.\n\nNo other behaviour changed: tool selection, the tool loop, storage and logging are as before.\n\n## Checks\n\nRun locally without the API (no requests sent, `data/athletes.json` not written):\n\n- The static block is byte-identical before and after appending a fact to the athlete in memory.\n- The context block does contain the new fact.\n- The static block is still identical on the next day with the same facts.\n- Only the static block carries `cache_control`.\n\n## Not verified / to check in the next logs\n\n- **Minimum cacheable length.** Sonnet caches only prefixes of about 1024 tokens or more.\n  The static instructions plus the core tools are roughly 1000 tokens by my estimate\n  (the old full block read ~1090 tokens). If the first real calls after this change show\n  `cache_creation_input_tokens: 0` and `input_tokens` ~1000 on every call, the static\n  part is under the minimum. In that case it needs to be padded with real content or\n  the cache dropped; I did not pad it.\n- **Tool set in the prefix.** Tools come before system in the cache prefix, and\n  `select_tools()` changes the tool list by keyword (e.g. adding `plan_week` or\n  `predict_race`). A message that adds a tool group still misses the cache. That is\n  separate from `save_fact`, and NOTES.md says the keyword filter is worth keeping, so I\n  left it. Moving the marker to the last tool would not fix it: the group change still\n  alters the prefix.\n\nI did not call the API, deploy, or send anything anywhere.\n"}}}
